        "message": "On-arm root cause pinned: controller reader lag trips the semantic isCurrent\n\npair-1-on-tfdiag (image b122c2a3, per-observation digest/TF/projection\ntimings + updateBounds lock-wait logs): the semantic layer is\nexonerated - every observation costs 3.7-5.4 ms and no updateBounds\nexceeded 15 ms. The command_expired reproduced at 0.833 m with one\n~165 ms controller cycle. The planner's global costmap received\nstamps 14.2/14.3/14.4 at walls .407/.457/.594 while the controller's\nlocal costmap got the same stamps in a burst at .596/.601/.606 - a\n~150-200 ms per-process reader saturation of controller_server. The\nreliable depth-8 history delivered the backlog in order, so the\nnewest observation queued behind stale ones already past the layer's\n500 ms isCurrent window; the local costmap went non-current and the\ncontroller's costmap-currency wait blocked its cycle past the 100 ms\ncommand authority.\n\nRemedy: the mask/points/timing subscriptions move to best-effort\nkeep-last(3) - under backlog the OLDEST observations drop, bounding\nthe newest observation's staleness by the stall itself; a dropped\ntriple component fails the digest join and is rejected exactly like\nany invalid observation. Fail-closed semantics and every threshold\nunchanged; label_info keeps its reliable transient-local latch."
      },
